title: 'The Warpline decision landscape at flight-readiness: what is actually the founder''s to call, and what only looks like consensus'
summary: 'Enumerated every open founder decision and every standing recommendation across the soundness audit, the F4 programme, the replacement epic and this session''s measurements — as preparation for a decision session. Two structural findings: there is NO live team consensus (the 200-row debate record is entirely auto-generated type:"complementary" nomination overlaps with zero conflicting positions, so it carries no signal), and one previously-listed founder call was resolved rather than decided, without moving the FG-3 freeze. The top-line decision changed shape: the contested-denominator question is no longer blocked on whether the mechanism works, because it now demonstrably does.'
