  - '#admit'
  - '#oracle'
  - '#grade'
  - '#warp-store'
  - '#f4-classifier'
  - '#warpline-cli'
  - '#weave'
  - '#essence-hash'
  - '#ts-lens'
learnings:
  - '"THE TEAM AGREES" WAS NEVER MEASURED HERE — the 200-row debate ledger is 200/200 type:"complementary", every row auto-generated from nomination overlap ("Multiple agents responded to event ev-…"), with no stance field and no conflicting position ever recorded. It is not a consensus instrument; it is a log of co-occurrence. The founder had already rejected "the team believes" as a gate on principle, and the data independently shows there was no signal there to reject. Any future claim of team agreement needs an instrument that can record DISAGREEMENT, or it measures nothing.'
  - 'A DECISION CAN BE DISSOLVED INSTEAD OF MADE. T-2026-07-21-005 listed the CLI/daemon `--claim` asymmetry as a founder call because closing it would "move descriptorsId and reset the FG-3 denominator". It did not: descriptorsId hashes VERB_DESCRIPTORS + NEXT_LEGAL_VERBS + the tool-name map, all in daemon/descriptors.ts, and the fix was CLI prose and option wiring only. Before scheduling a decision, check whether its stated cost is actually incurred — the cost was inherited, not verified.'
  - 'AN ''UNMEASURED'' THAT TRACES TO ONE ROOT IS ONE DECISION, NOT MANY. Every falsifier on the standing report reads unmeasured, and all of them reduce to the same fact: this repo has a single writer, so it structurally cannot produce a contested verdict. The apparent breadth of open questions was one decision (where the denominator comes from) wearing several costumes.'
  - PROVING THE MECHANISM CHANGES WHICH DECISION IS TOP-LINE. Before the dress rehearsal, 'where does the denominator come from' competed with 'does the contested path even work'. The rehearsal answered the second, which promoted the first from one-of-many to the item everything else waits on. Sequencing decisions is downstream of removing uncertainty, not parallel to it.
