body: |-
  PREPARED FOR A DECISION SESSION. This entry is the landscape as measured on 2026-08-11, so the session itself has a durable starting point and the decisions can be recorded against it.

  FOUNDER DECISIONS, GROUPED BY WHAT THEY GATE.

  Gating the field test:
   1. WHERE THE FIRST CONTESTED DENOMINATOR COMES FROM. Newly sharp. The mechanism is proven end-to-end (genesis -> fork x2 -> propose x2 -> FAST_ADMIT -> KNOT -> resolve, plus byte-identical restore at depth 41), so the blocker is no longer capability — it is that this repo has ONE writer and a serial human cannot manufacture concurrency. Candidate sources: the Expo field-test project, a driven swarm, or a synthetic harness.
   2. REPLICATION / states/. One fabric, one disk, one manual backup verb; a lost state file is a permanent fail-closed for that base and nothing re-derives it. The audit named this the top-line risk and it has been open since P2.

  Gating the F4 measurement (all from T-2026-07-21-005):
   3. FG-2 — the truncated-descriptions arm, and whether the >=80% bar applies to it or it is observational.
   4. FG-3 — the descriptor freeze + denominator-reset rule; the task's own instruction is to do a descriptor REVIEW PASS BEFORE pinning, because every later fix is expensive.
   5. FG-4 — stratified KNOT seed corpus: strata are named, COUNTS are undecided.
   6. The stopping rule and n — without it, optional stopping voids the number however well the instrument is frozen.
   7. Both-skins ambiguity — must the non-Claude family appear on both arms? A day of harness work plus procurement rides on one sentence.
   8. The two remaining CLI-arm asymmetries (daemon `status`, `shadow.tail` — neither has a CLI equivalent). Closing either DOES move descriptorsId. The third listed asymmetry (`propose --claim`) was resolved 2026-08-11 without moving the freeze.

  Product shape:
   9. LAYER OR REPLACEMENT. T-2026-07-01-007 is an epic to make Warpline byte-authoritative; the team's own readiness panel scored ~0.05. Loid's A7 review recommends hard-deferring remote/sync and shipping MIRROR MODE as the product.
   10. MOAT-SILENCE ITSELF. The moat memo locates the moat in per-codebase calibration, which a specification cannot leak — so silence may be buying nothing while costing permanently-cold agents, an entire falsifier programme, and a procurement problem.
   11. WHETHER AGENTS CAN REACH THE GATED PATH — three recorded options: expose the base-minting verb; accept that the gate guards the human door and source the agent denominator from the native write path; or move the gate. Adding a verb changes what the cold-agent test measures.

  Safety, before any swarm:
   12. TIER-0 INVARIANT CONFLICTS (T-2026-06-24-015) — disjoint-but-jointly-wrong changes auto-weave at Tier 0 with zero review; "no graph knot" is being trusted as "safe".
   13. THE OVER-BLOCK CEILING (T-2026-07-15-008) — measured 3/3 on Move-3: commuting edits contend the same caller essence and produce a false KNOT. Options: essence granularity, BRUSH demotion, or ranking-side mitigation.
   14. INJECTION DEFENCE SCOPE (T-2026-06-24-013) — the envelope shipped; the acceptance criterion is a BLIND, externally-authored red-team corpus scored by someone who did not write the payloads.

  STANDING RECOMMENDATIONS (owners and evidence exist; these need scheduling, not adjudication): use alongside git never instead until P0 closes (audit); hard-defer M4 remote/sync and ship mirror mode (Loid A7); branching model + walkable history graph (Cid + Jinx, T-2026-07-01-017); relax the H1 guard so multi-agent work does not serialize to one merge per generation at N>=3 (T-2026-07-01-030 — the stated blocker, MergeRecipe, already shipped); lift top-level const units in the TS lens (T-2026-07-15-005 — false-equal shaped, and an Expo app is full of exported consts); re-run the six auditors' original demonstrations against HEAD (nothing is verified closed, only mapped to commits).

  MY RANKING, RECORDED SO IT CAN BE CHECKED LATER: the denominator decision should not wait, because every "unmeasured" on the standing report reduces to it. T-2026-07-01-030 (the H1 guard) is the one to pull forward before the field test, because at N>=3 the swarm would serialize and the run would measure a known bottleneck instead of the product.
